BT /F1 11 Tf 50 780 Td 14 TL (Certainly! Below is a simple Python implementation of the **Bubble Sort** algorithm, which you can run locally without any internet access. It sorts the array `[1,5,6,7,8,9,10,4,3]` in ascending order.) Tj T* (PYTHON) Tj T* (def bubble_sort\(arr\):) Tj T* (    n = len\(arr\)) Tj T* (    # Traverse through all array elements) Tj T* (    for i in range\(n\):) Tj T* (        # Last i elements are already in place) Tj T* (        for j in range\(0, n - i - 1\):) Tj T* (            # Swap if the element found is greater than the next element) Tj T* (            if arr[j] > arr[j + 1]:) Tj T* (                arr[j], arr[j + 1] = arr[j + 1], arr[j]) Tj T* (    return arr) Tj T* (# Example array) Tj T* (array = [1, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 4, 3]) Tj T* (# Sorting the array) Tj T* (sorted_array = bubble_sort\(array\)) Tj T* (print\("Sorted array:", sorted_array\)) Tj T* (**Explanation:**) Tj T* (1. **`bubble_sort\(arr\)`** iterates over the list multiple times.) Tj T* (2. In each pass, adjacent elements are compared and swapped if they are out of order.) Tj T* (3. After each full pass, the largest unsorted element ?bubbles up? to its correct position.) Tj T* (4. The process repeats until no swaps are needed, indicating the list is sorted.) Tj T* (Running this code will output:) Tj T* (CODE) Tj T* (Sorted array: [1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10]) Tj T* (Feel free to modify the array or try other sorting algorithms \(e.g., Insertion Sort, Selection Sort\) if you?d like! ?) Tj T* ET
